messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_pixarlog.c
Line: 1507
Function: PixarLogCleanup
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: PixarLogCleanup dereferences sp->tbuf without verifying that sp (cast from tif->tif_data) is non-NULL. The preceding guarded block only protects the inflateEnd/deflateEnd calls; the later 'if (sp->tbuf)' runs unconditionally. If the cleanup hook is called when tif->tif_data is NULL (e.g., after a prior cleanup), this leads to a NULL pointer dereference and crash.

Source context:
```c
     1467:          * a TransferFunction is set. The size of the TransferFunction
     1468:          * depends on 1<<bitspersample. So if we increase it, an access
     1469:          * out of the buffer will happen at directory flushing.
     1470:          * Another option would be to clear those targs.
     1471:          */
     1472:         td->td_bitspersample = 8;
     1473:         td->td_sampleformat = SAMPLEFORMAT_UINT;
     1474:     }
     1475: }
